@page "/spaces/{SpaceId:guid}"

@using Yello.Client.Spaces

@inject IStringLocalizer<ClientCopy> Localizer
@inject SpaceNarration Narration

@*
    A SPACE'S HOME - THE FIRST SPACE-SCOPED CLIENT ROUTE. AC4, AC9, AC10 of 1.7; UX-DR31, UX-DR32.

    THE ARRIVAL IS SpaceArrival's (story 2.2, Task 10), shared with the Board so its rules exist once:
    nothing is asked about a Space the switcher did not list; nothing renders before the server has
    answered; both 404 causes render one refusal surface; a 401 is YelloApiHandler's; a first arrival
    focuses the heading; and a re-arrival in the same Space - choosing it again in the switcher - keeps
    the page and an open form's text while the Role is re-read (story 2.2, AC14; deferred-work.md:481).
    Space home used to reset all of that on every parameter set, which dropped a typed Project name.

    THE HEADING DOES NOT NAME THE SPACE - the context bar does, and the name lives in one place.

    SPACE SETTINGS is linked from the context bar since story 3.1 (AC4, open question 4 (a)), not from here - so an
    empty Space offers exactly one action besides "Leave this Space" at the foot, which every Role but the Owner is
    offered here because Space settings is not theirs. The empty-state case sets it aside deliberately. A Role re-read
    lower on that page is narrated, then
    routed here, and this page says the sentence on arrival (UX-DR29). The sentence belongs to that Space: this page is
    reused when the switcher moves to another Space's home, and drops it then (story 3.2, AC11).

    THE PROJECTS (story 2.1) are ProjectList's, rendered only once the Space has answered, keyed on the
    Space so a switch starts a new list rather than reusing the departed one's. A 404 the list or a
    creation meets renders the one refusal surface. Each row links to its Board (story 2.2).
*@

@* Rendered empty from this page's first render and filled once the Space has answered (story 4.4, ledger :550,
   Q15 (a)): a status region inserted already holding its sentence is not announced by every screen reader. Only when
   there is a sentence to say, so a page that says nothing - a refusal included - is exactly as it was (AD-3). *@
@if (_narration is not null)
{
    <p class="space-home__narration" role="status">@_shown</p>
}

<SpaceArrival SpaceId="@SpaceId" Context="arrival">
    <div class="space-home">
        <PageHeading>@Localizer["SpaceHomeHeading"]</PageHeading>

        <AfterArrival OnArrived="ShowNarration" />

        <ProjectList @key="SpaceId" SpaceId="@SpaceId" RoleCode="@arrival.Current.Role" OnSpaceRefused="arrival.Refuse" />

        <LeaveSpaceSection SpaceId="@SpaceId" RoleCode="@arrival.Current.Role" OnSpaceRefused="arrival.Refuse" />
    </div>
</SpaceArrival>

@code {
    private string? _narration;
    private string? _shown;
    private Guid _narratedIn;

    /// <summary>
    /// The Space this route names.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid SpaceId { get; set; }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _narration = Narration.Take();
        _narratedIn = SpaceId;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// This page is reused across Spaces, so the sentence it took goes with the Space it was said about (story 3.2,
    /// AC11; UX-DR38): another Space's home says nothing about the last one.
    /// </summary>
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (SpaceId != _narratedIn)
        {
            _narration = null;
            _shown = null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The Space has answered: the sentence carried here from Space settings is written into the region now, a browser
    /// task after the region was rendered empty.
    /// </summary>
    private void ShowNarration()
    {
        if (_narration is not null && SpaceId == _narratedIn)
        {
            _shown = _narration;
        }
    }
}
